{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-80668",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(0,1)\\times (0,1)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,1)\\times (1,2).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =(1-0){\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+({\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+({x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1})\\cdot ({e}^{y}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =1+1\\cdot ({e}^{2}-{e}^{1}) \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2}-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
